# 7. Linux Package Management

## `apt update`

Refreshes local package information from configured repositories.

```bash
sudo apt update
```

## `apt upgrade`

Installs newer versions of packages that are already installed.

```bash
sudo apt upgrade
```

## Installing a package

```bash
sudo apt install package-name
```

## Removing a package

```bash
sudo apt remove package-name
```

### Key Difference

```text
apt update
→ Refresh package information

apt upgrade
→ Upgrade installed packages
```

