# 8. DNS Records

DNS translates domain/hostnames into network information.

Important DNS record types:

| Record | Purpose                               |
| ------ | ------------------------------------- |
| A      | Maps hostname to IPv4 address         |
| AAAA   | Maps hostname to IPv6 address         |
| CNAME  | Creates an alias for another hostname |
| MX     | Identifies mail servers for a domain  |
| TXT    | Stores text/verification information  |

### A Record Example

```text
example.com
      ↓
A Record
      ↓
IPv4 Address
```

### MX Record

An MX record identifies the mail server responsible for receiving email for a domain.

MX records are particularly important when troubleshooting email services such as Exchange Online.

